{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1492487-alternative-integrity-traits-for-splats","id":1492487,"title":"Alternative Integrity traits for splats","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-09-06T23:40:56-07:00","id":1492487,"title":"Alternative Integrity traits for splats","content":"I was wondering how changing the Integrity-like traits of splats, by switching them with those from other splats or creating new ones, would affect the themes and focus of respective game lines.<br /> I think some combinations may actually make sense and even have interesting results.<br /> <br /> I'll start :<br /> <b>Demon: Memory</b> (aka Programming?)<br /> <br /> What if the Fall wasn't a specific event, but a gradual experience? Just as Memory is, among other things, a measure of a mummy's sense of identity and free will against being a slave to the Judge's will, Demons too may struggle to gradually letting go of the God Machine 's chains, with the risk of relapsing","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26440,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26440-moonwhisper","user":"moonwhisper","date":". 09-10-2022, 10:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26440-moonwhisper","name":"moonwhisper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26440_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-07T00:29:06-07:00","id":1492489,"title":"","content":"Hmm...<br /> <br /> <b>Vampire <span style=\"color:#252C2F\">\u2014 </span>Cover</b>: Don't let people know you are an undead predator. Twist is that 'people' includes yourself. Fake it till you make it.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><b>Demon \u2014 Pilgrimage</b>: Pave your own road to Hell with good intentions. Experience the full human existence, with all its zeniths and nadirs.<br /> <br /> <b>Promethean \u2014 Stability</b>: You are unborn, incomplete, unstable. Ground your fires with hope for tomorrow, and occasionally venting out some steam.<br /> <br /> <b>Deviant \u2014 Clarity</b>: It happened, and you did it. Don't let Them tell otherwise. Take control of your own past to seize the future, this time on your terms.<br /> <br /> <b>Changeling \u2014 Memory</b>: Remember what life was like, before it all went widdershins. Remember yourself so that you become yours, not Theirs.<br /> <br /> <b>Mummy \u2014 Wisdom</b>: Reflect upon the cruelty you and your masters inflict on the world. Lament, repent, and take responsibility.<br /> <br /> <b>Mage \u2014 Satiety</b>: Feast upon the world's Mysteries and lose yourself in trance. Fast until your Obsessions take a life on their own to push you to the next Mystery.<br /> <br /> <b>Beast \u2014 Synergy</b>: Cooperate with your Horror Within such that you may better understand, and eventually shape, the stories you tell and hear about yourself.<br /> <br /> <b>Geist \u2014 Harmony</b>: Stay too dead, and you risk being stuck. Stay too alive, and you risk being powerless. Always remember you are both.<br /> <br /> <b>Werewolf \u2014 Humanity</b>: The Wolf must Hunt, but the Man must Hold. Hold on to what you held dear, even if the Hunt washes it away.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-07T09:34:43-07:00","id":1492522,"title":"","content":"<b>Humanity</b>-Arguably all of them, but if we had to get picky, Promethean, Changeling, Beast, Hunter, and Mage are probably the games where this'd be the most useful and interesting. The laziest answer is <b>Promethean</b>, but that doesn't make it inappropriate.<br /> <br /> <b>Harmony</b>-Any splat that deals with a more overt duality benefits from this, so arguably Geist, Changeling, Beast are easy correlations on that front. Interesting cases could be made for Mage and Promethean as well, depending on how you read their journey. Still, <b>Geist</b> is the appropriate (if easy) mark, so.<br /> <br /> <b>Wisdom</b>-Just about any splat that has to deal with power as a mechanical theme warrants it, so Demon and Mummy are easy picks. It also does a good job reflecting the personal responsibility any Beast has over the managing of their developing lair and the consequences of not keeping a firm grip on it, so there's that. Interesting things also happen with Werewolf and Hunter, but because it's not only appropriate but interesting, I think <b>Beast</b> is the clear winner on this one.<br /> <br /> <b>Pilgrimage</b>-Pilgrimage is a good stat for anyone with a larger scale goal consideration, or otherwise inverts the spending argument by starting low and ideally trending high. Changeling, Demon, Geist, and Mummy all fit in that model pretty well. There's an interesting take of Deviant as well that could come out of that, particularly with some Light of the Sun context. Arguably, Geist is the one where reaching the end through growth matters most, but since I'm trying to keep a complete shuffle, <b>Demon</b> is the more interesting one of the remaining.<br /> <br /> <b>Clarity</b>-&quot;Honey, where are my keys/pants?&quot; Anyhow, Mage's relationship to vision makes that a superficially easy pick, but actually engaging with the deeper ideas....Hunter and Deviant also make for interesting relationships. Mummy also plays nicely. There's a really <i>wild</i> version of Beast that emerges from this take, but out of those, I think <b>Mummy</b>'s relationship with the Judges and everything behind and around that makes this the winner.<br /> <br /> <b>Coded Integrity</b>-Arguably, the more &quot;human&quot; the splat, the more appropriate. Mage is easy in that regards, Vampire and Geist are also considerations, as is Deviant. There's something interesting in Changeling also engaging with it. That said, <b>Mage </b>engaging with something like the Code and then falling away from it is the most interesting, I think.<br /> <br /> <b>Synergy</b>-See the overt duality argument, and be unsurprised to see Werewolf, Changeling, and Beast here, Vampire too, now that I dwell on it. Mummy to, at an odd angle. We'll go lazy and say <b>Werewolf</b>.<br /> <br /> <b>Memory</b>-Memory plays well when the sands of time should be a thing to consider, so Vampire and Demon play nice here. Changeling too, particularly since it can more immediately play into the relevances of their day to day life. Geist can get interesting with this via the lens of death. Finally, there's a whole section in a potential Chronicler's Guide for a Beast with Memory. Honestly though, there's something delicious for the fairy tale to interact with Memory, and it has thematics that can play nicely with what Clarity was doing, so I think I'd have to give this to <b>Changeling</b>.<br /> <br /> <b>Cover</b>-It's all about who's interested in drawing up lines and veils and masks and distance. Changeling and Hunter come to mind, as does Deviant. Vampire could easily translate it over into the Mask and Dirge dichotomy. Geist has some tangential relationship via Hide From Reapers, but that's a little weak. Of these, though, <b>Deviant's</b> probably the one that most benefits from having multiple of the same meter, and the way Variations can easily degrade those makes a neat tie in.<br /> <br /> <b>Satiety/Kinship</b>-Arguably another &quot;all of them case&quot;, but the combo of balancing hunger and close relationships is so obviously an ur-sample for Conviction and Loyalty to draw from that Deviant stands out. Werewolf and Mage also have some easy draws. Same with Hunter. Vampire is also a great place ot see how this archetypal take works-in fact, so much so, I'mma give it to <b>Vampire</b>.<br /> <br /> <b>Stability</b>-Just about anything that calls for constant stressors works here, so Hunter, Changeling, and Promethean are all easy picks here. Werewolf and Geist also have interesting consequences here as well. Still, <b>Hunter</b> probably the one that gets the most out of more directly interacting with their psychological state as damage, so here we are.<br /> <br /> Obviously, about half of this is sincere, if short, consideration, and the other half is really lazy spitballing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 09-07-2022, 12:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-08T18:29:24-07:00","id":1492654,"title":"","content":"My take from this is actually that not only any splat could work with any of them, if some requiring more work or lending itself to more specific themes, but that actually making adaptations so any splat may work under any Integrity-like stat has another benefit: it makes for an easier time defining a theme for your <i>chronicle</i> while keeping it open to mixed splats (as either PCs or NPCs).<br /> <br /> Tying the stat to the chronicle means that you have a solid core theme, and you can welcome different splats as they add their views to the same theme instead of despite the theme. Everyone uses <b>Humanity</b> and you have a game about the need to stay connected to the species you don't belong to anymore. Everyone uses <b>Wisdom</b> and you have a game about how distinct ways to power still hold the same basic ethical questions on using it. Everyone uses <b>Satiety</b> and you have indeed a game about monsters forming kinship over the common experience of living with unnatural needs, <i>even hunters</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-08T18:50:27-07:00","id":1492655,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1492487-alternative-integrity-traits-for-splats?p=1492654#post1492654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My take from this is actually that not only any splat could work with any of them, if some requiring more work or lending itself to more specific themes, but that actually making adaptations so any splat may work under any Integrity-like stat has another benefit: it makes for an easier time defining a theme for your <i>chronicle</i> while keeping it open to mixed splats (as either PCs or NPCs).<br /> <br /> Tying the stat to the chronicle means that you have a solid core theme, and you can welcome different splats as they add their views to the same theme instead of despite the theme. Everyone uses <b>Humanity</b> and you have a game about the need to stay connected to the species you don't belong to anymore. Everyone uses <b>Wisdom</b> and you have a game about how distinct ways to power still hold the same basic ethical questions on using it. Everyone uses <b>Satiety</b> and you have indeed a game about monsters forming kinship over the common experience of living with unnatural needs, <i>even hunters</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would also argue that that's the case, yes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-08T19:27:25-07:00","id":1492659,"title":"","content":"The idea of using Integrity equivalents as a Chronicle feature instead of a supernatural creature type feature is certainly appealing. Though I'm imaging the amount of work it would take to implement with the current state of many of them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-09T19:20:19-07:00","id":1492732,"title":"","content":"A lot of work, but now that's something I want from a 3rd edition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-09T20:55:40-07:00","id":1492734,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1492487-alternative-integrity-